{% extends "page/checkout/order.html.twig" %}

{#
    Sprint 06 — single active payment method.

    When the shop offers exactly one usable payment method, the order page's
    "payment method" block has nothing to say and nowhere useful to lead: the
    pencil inside it goes back to a selection page that no longer renders. The
    whole block is left out, heading and method line included.

    Shipping is a sibling block, decided separately — see sprint 07 below. With
    several carriers its pencil is still the way to change the delivery set.

    The condition is answered by payment-base's OrderController extension; with
    two or more methods it is false and the block renders exactly as core does.
#}
{% block checkout_order_payment_method %}
    {% if not oView.isSinglePaymentAutoAssigned() %}
        {{ parent() }}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{#
    Sprint 07 — single active shipping method (revised 2026-08-31).

    Originally the whole carrier block went. That also removed the line naming
    the carrier, so the order page — the page the customer confirms — no longer
    said how the goods were coming. With one delivery set there is nothing to
    decide, but there is still something to know.

    Now only the edit control goes. The heading and
    `checkout_order_shipping_carrier_desc` (which prints the set's title off
    `oView.getShipSet()`) render as core wrote them; the pencil, and the form
    that would post back to `cl=payment`, do not. Shown, not changeable.

    That the pencil goes matters beyond tidiness: with one delivery set and one
    payment method the payment step redirects straight back here (sprint 07 S6
    D1), so the pencil led into a bounce. With several payment methods it would
    have landed on a step whose carrier selector is now read-only anyway.

    Payment is decided separately — the two blocks are siblings and either can
    be reduced without the other.
#}
{% block checkout_order_shipping_carrier_form %}
    {% if not oView.isSingleShippingAutoAssigned() %}
        {{ parent() }}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
